      "text": [
        ": «أَرْبَعُ صَلَوَاتٍُ يُصَلِّيهَا اَلرَّجُلُ فِي كُلِّ سَاعَةٍ صَلاَةٌ فَاتَتْكَ فَمَتَى مَا ذَكَرْتَهَا أَدَّيْتَهَا وَ صَلاَةُ رَكْعَتَيْ طَوَافِ اَلْفَرِيضَةِ وَ صَلاَةُ اَلْكُسُوفِ وَ اَلصَّلاَةُ عَلَى اَلْمَيِّتِ هَذِهِ يُصَلِّيهِنَّ اَلرَّجُلُ فِي اَلسَّاعَاتِ كُلِّهَا."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Zurarah narrated from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) that He said:\n\"There are four prayers that a person may perform at any hour: a prayer that you missed, so whenever you remember it, you perform it; the two units (rak'ahs) of the obligatory circumambulation (Tawaf) prayer; the prayer for an eclipse (Salat al-Kusuf); and the prayer over a deceased person (Salat al-Janazah). These prayers can be performed by a person at any time.\""
        ]
      }
    },
